pieboot (0.1.2) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * GICv3 interrupts convert as a GICv2's do, and with a GICv3 EL1 gets
    the GIC's system registers.
  * A DesignWare or 16550 UART can be the console.
  * pieboot.ramcons=BASE,SIZE also writes the console to RAM that survives
    a reset.
  * pieboot.fallback=1 arms a DesignWare watchdog on a board without the
    firmware mailbox.
  * EL1 gets the PMU and debug registers without traps to EL2.
  * A trap to EL2 other than a PSCI call is skipped instead of retried.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:30:00 +0000

pieboot (0.1.1) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * pieboot.fallback=1 in the boot-args sets the firmware's tryboot flag and
    arms the watchdog, so that a hang, a panic or any reset can boot
    tryboot.txt.
  * The firmware mailbox gives up after a second without an answer.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:26:38 +0000

